# Kidora — always read the project report first

**Before doing anything in this repo, read `PROJECT-REPORT.md` at the repo root.**
It is the reverse-engineered reference for this codebase (architecture, data model,
user flow, UI system, verified defect list, conventions). Do not re-derive that
context by exploring — read the report, then explore only what the task needs.

If you discover the report is wrong or out of date, update `PROJECT-REPORT.md` in the
same change.

## Non-negotiables

- **Arabic RTL first.** All user-facing copy is Arabic; `<html dir="rtl">`. New strings
  must be Arabic and must be checked in RTL layout.
- **Escape every output with `h()`** (`htmlspecialchars` wrapper in `includes/functions.php`).
- **Prepared statements only.** The single interpolated `ORDER BY` is whitelist-guarded;
  keep that idiom, never interpolate raw input.
- **POST-redirect-GET.** POST handlers end with `header('Location: <self>'); exit;` and
  pass state through `$_SESSION['flash_*']` keys.
- **No build step.** Plain PHP 8 + PDO, vanilla JS, no framework/Composer/npm. Do not
  introduce a toolchain without being asked.

## Page contract

```php
require_once __DIR__ . '/config/db.php';
require_once __DIR__ . '/includes/functions.php';
$child = require_login();
$progress = ensure_daily_progress($pdo, $child['id']);
// POST handling → redirect
$__pageTitle = '...'; $__pageLine = '...';   // $__pageLine = what the companion says
require_once __DIR__ . '/includes/header.php';
require_once __DIR__ . '/includes/navbar.php';
// markup
require_once __DIR__ . '/includes/footer.php';
```

## Styling

`assets/css/main.css` holds shared tokens/components; page-specific CSS goes in that
page's own inline `<style>` block. `includes/navbar.php` and `includes/footer.php` are
self-contained (HTML + CSS + JS in one file).

**The animated background must stay dark.** Every text colour on top of it is light,
so brightening the background makes text vanish as the gradient animates — this was a
real bug (worst case 1.1:1) and is now fixed by three interacting pieces:
`MAX_BG_LUMINANCE` in `assets/js/theme-engine.js`, the `#animated-bg::after` scrim,
and the capped `glowPulse` opacity — all documented in `PROJECT-REPORT.md` §4 and §8.
The binding constraint is `--text-muted` `#b9abd4` at 4.87:1. If you change any of the
three, re-measure contrast against the **lightest** phase of the 12 s loop for every
character before claiming it works.

Never use the `background` shorthand on gradient-clipped text (`background-clip:text`)
— it resets the clip and the gradient renders as a solid box. Use `background-image`.

## Run locally

`php -S localhost:8000` — SQLite is created and seeded on first request.
Admin at `/admin/login.php` (`admin@kidora.com` / `admin123`). Reset by deleting
`storage/kidora.sqlite`.

## Known-defect awareness

`PROJECT-REPORT.md` §8 lists the verified defects, marking which are resolved.
Do not "fix" an open item as a drive-by; confirm it is in scope first.

Two things future work keeps getting wrong:

- **All seed content lives in `database/seed.php`.** The schema files are
 structure-only. They used to carry their own `INSERT` blocks that ran first and
 made most of `seed.php` dead code — do not put data back into them.
- **Adding a game mechanic takes three edits**: a `run*()` branch in
 `assets/js/games-engine.js`, an entry in `game_types()` (`includes/functions.php`),
 and seed rows. Admin dropdowns and POST validation both follow `game_types()`.

The mission package is `tasks` → `tasks.figure_id` → `tasks.game_type`, and all three
are meant to be about the same subject. Resolve the figure with `figure_for_task()`,
never with a random query.
